Reading it: pure descent leaves everything where it started, so
'stayed' would be near 100% and the answer would be right only as
often as the start was -- about a third. Pure classification makes
the predicted well independent of the start, so every row of the
matrix would be the same and would reproduce the native well
frequencies (g- 50.2%, t 32.9%, g+ 16.9%). The gap between the two
conditional rates above is how much the start still matters once
the rule has run.

